==================================================
1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE
==================================================

Develop a working real-time hardware monitoring and detection prototype for AetherHound.

The objective is to capture live electromagnetic RF signals and acoustic signals from a monitored environment, process both streams continuously, and identify unusual signal patterns while acquisition is running.

This is NOT a simple recording application.

The application must continuously acquire, process, analyze and detect signals in real time.

Week 1 has exactly TWO primary modules:

MODULE 1: HARDWARE SETUP + REAL-TIME RF AND ACOUSTIC MONITORING

MODULE 2: BENIGN CPU FAN MORSE-CODE SIMULATOR + REAL-TIME PATTERN DETECTION

The two modules must work independently and together.

The application must work with actual hardware when connected.

A separate test mode must allow detection testing without physical SDR hardware.

Do not build the React dashboard, FastAPI platform, database, ML autoencoder, advanced threat intelligence or other future-week components.

