4. REAL-TIME RF ACQUISITION
==================================================

Create:

hardware/rf_capture.py

Objective:

Continuously capture actual RF IQ samples using RTL-SDR and send them to the RF processing engine.

Implementation requirements:

1. Initialize RTL-SDR.
2. Configure center frequency.
3. Configure supported sample rate.
4. Configure RF gain.
5. Configure frequency correction where applicable.
6. Use continuous asynchronous sample acquisition.
7. Use read_samples_async() or an equivalent supported continuous acquisition method.
8. Process incoming IQ sample chunks.
9. Timestamp every processing window.
10. Maintain a bounded buffer.
11. Avoid blocking the acquisition callback with expensive processing.
12. Send sample chunks to a thread-safe processing queue.
13. Handle device disconnection.
14. Support graceful stop and cleanup.

Use configurable defaults appropriate for the connected RTL-SDR.

RF CONFIGURATION:

- Center frequency.
- Sample rate.
- Gain.
- FFT size.
- Samples per processing window.
- Detection update interval.

Validate hardware-supported configuration values.

Do not transmit RF signals.

The SDR must operate in receive-only mode.

A. LIVE RF SPECTRUM PROCESSING

For every incoming sample window:

1. Apply a suitable window function.
2. Calculate FFT.
3. Calculate power spectrum.
4. Convert power to dB.
5. Estimate the local noise floor.
6. Identify spectral peaks.
7. Calculate peak-to-noise-floor deviation.
8. Track frequency changes over time.
9. Identify unusual signal bursts.
10. Update the live RF monitoring output.

Use proper frequency-bin calculations based on actual center frequency and sampling rate.

B. RF ANOMALY DETECTION

Create:

detection/rf_detector.py

Implement real-time statistical detection.

The detector should:

- Learn a rolling baseline from observed RF spectrum windows.
- Maintain robust median and median absolute deviation statistics.
- Identify significant spectral deviations.
- Detect persistent unusual frequency peaks.
- Detect sudden unexpected power changes.
- Detect unusual periodic signal activity where measurable.
- Avoid flagging every small fluctuation.
- Support configurable thresholds.
- Apply minimum-duration and persistence checks.
- Use hysteresis to avoid repeated alert flickering.

Generate an RF detection event when a configurable anomaly condition is met.

Example:

[AETHERHOUND RF ALERT]

Event: Unusual RF Spectral Activity
Sensor: SDR-01
Frequency: Detected frequency
Signal Level: Measured power
Noise Floor: Estimated noise floor
Deviation: Calculated deviation
Timestamp: Actual timestamp
Status: SUSPICIOUS RF ACTIVITY

Do not claim that an RF spike proves covert data transmission.

C. LIVE RF WATERFALL

Maintain a rolling history of processed RF spectra.

Display:

- Frequency axis.
- Time axis.
- Signal intensity.
- Persistent spectral activity.
- Anomaly markers.

Use a bounded history to prevent excessive memory consumption.

